  "id": "mental-synthesis",
  "term": "mental synthesis",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, mental synthesis is the combining of elements in consciousness so that some contents take the form of, or help form, others. It can include such processes as fusion, association, recognition, and the awareness of identity or resemblance, viewed in terms of how presented elements come together.",
